I. Code_embedding_local

You can find in Code_embedding_local the Retrieved Augmented Generation model

You first need to read "environment.txt", then "requirements.txt" (read it!), then install them
Then start Qdrant with docker

Then use index_html.py to create a Qdrant Collection

Then you can use the ask_LLM and code_LLM functions

In test_zone you can create .txt files with the generated codes and then check them with test_code.py

tools gives you a few utilitarian functions to interact with the collection

II. Improvement

You can find in improvement the original project of improvement and testing, with new TOML files for Maude and corrected AI-generated tests since some of them were broken and caused some codes to fail even if they were working